unts, orders, customers, reviews, sales summaries, campaigns, storefront drafts and shipping profiles are all exposed, and the destructive half is deliberately absent, with no delete tool for a product or a discount, no refund or payout tool, no way to email a buyer, products created unpublished with publishing a separate request, and storefront writes carrying a revision check that rejects a stale draft instead of overwriting a colleague's edit. Two details worth carrying: money arrives in minor units, 1999 is 19.99, and the read tools see buyer names and addresses which then travel to whichever model provider the merchant connected. Held with the class named: BACKLNK on the technical SEO, AEO and GEO audit class carried by Seo Audit Console, Geolint, CiteRank, Seomely, AEO Engine, AIO.GEO and MisarSEO, despite its keyless endpoint answering 200 with six tools and fourteen checks plus a verify_fixes loop, which is the best mechanism in that class this month and still a name in a class with seven owners; Subastum on the geo-niche auction class owned by Subastech, a Spanish BOE and Social Security auction reader with scope subastum.lectura and a total-cost-of-a-bid calculation, with the reversal test named as a driven session showing the state portal answers a question the judicial one cannot; Xcout Intel on company intelligence beside Synorb, FinzData, SimilarLabs and Velarion at roughly 450,000 companies across 115 countries with per-claim provenance; GSC Magic on Search Console, Bing and GA4 analytics, a prior disposition three passes running; Odds-API.io on consumer sports data; PastCharts on app store and trends data beside Sonar ASO, AppSigma and TrendPulse; Scenes on media generation; chromeleon-mcp on anti-detect browser automation where Veilus set the ruling; etrink on the crypto and trading class; Graphlog Career on career tooling; Nightshift Labs on x402-paid security checks; Addness and Apogee Ads as prior dispositions; PuraSIM on travel eSIM; and All My 