Evening sweep November 5 2026, fired on the 21:00 MST tick ten hours after the late morning read, and the two named surfaces separated cleanly. The mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap canonical returned set-identical to the 11:01 MST capture: 19,513 server URLs after stripping the locale prefixes, zero additions and zero removals, the second exact empty diff in one day and the first time this surface has produced two in the same day. The counting note from the previous pass still holds and still matters: a raw union reads 28,851 URLs and 9,338 of them are marketing, topic and search pages, so only the /servers/ subset of 19,513 is the server universe, and /all answered 403 for the fifth consecutive pass, a standing condition rather than an incident. mcp.so carried the whole window and carried it without the stale-read trap of the previous pass: the plain and cache-busted reads returned the same 172 timestamped cards, parsing to 140 card objects across 117 distinct slugs with the same newest stamp 2026-11-06T02:14:00.852Z, and 13 entries above the late morning stamp of 2026-11-05T17:29:38.960Z reduced to 10 distinct servers once the duplicate renderings were collapsed. The submission queue added 23 items from 6809 to 6831, one a listing update for brewpage-mcp and five a single author's SEO fleet under the single-author rule. Two servers were catalogued, each on a gap rather than a name. Ripplewatch MCP - https://www.ripplewatch.ai/api/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP, registered as ai.ripplewatch/ripplewatch 0.1.0 and active since 2026-10-21T04:13:37Z, OAuth through the vendor's Supabase authorization server with authorization_code and refresh_token grants, dynamic client registration and both S256 and plain advertised for PKCE. A keyless initialize returns 401 with a body reading Authentication required and a WWW-Authenticate header naming its protected-resource document, so the tier is documentation rather than a driven session. It scores ten inputs each from -100 to +100 - hiring, pricing activity, product changes, press and funding, relevance trend, win rate against you, review sentiment, Reddit and Hacker News buzz, plus opt-in GitHub and ad activity - into five labels with below -15 Cooling and above +15 Heating up and a low-confidence marker when the data is thin, and it earns the guide because the three competitive intelligence entries here read only the public web while this one scores that web against the customer's own positioning, ICP and closed deals, fed six ways including a CRM CSV, an email forward address and an assistant reading closed deals from a tool it can already reach. Pricing is 29 dollars a month plus prepaid usage from a 50 dollar balance, first charge 79, no seat fee, refundable within 30 days, with both answers and each tracked competitor drawing from the balance, and the limits recorded are no published tool names, no SOC 2 by the vendor's own statement, business context sent to Anthropic models per request and plain PKCE offered beside S256. LoadOptimizer MCP - https://mcp.loadoptimizer.ai/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP gated by OAuth through the vendor web app, its protected-resource document naming a Supabase authorization server with scope email, a keyless initialize returning 401 with an empty body, and no official registry record on three searches. It is the first load-planning surface in the catalog: the logistics corner held Fitralo for carrier search, HaulierScope for GB operator licences, Container Tracking for shipments and PackIndex for packaging costs, and nothing answered what fits, in what order and what is left over. The assistant checks a request, plans the load, follows it to completion, reports per carrier what fit and what did not, and in Claude and ChatGPT renders the plan as a 3D view inside the conversation with stacking rules as an editable matrix; approval covers the account, full access versus read-only, public share links off unless ticked and which app is asking; and the honest cost is not the free tier but EUR 99.99 a month, because the connector needs a plan that includes API access and API access starts at Pro, against a 10-day full Pro trial with no card. Limits recorded: quota and request rate shared with API keys, actions attributed to the approving user tagged via agent, tool-level analytics with an assistant-written goal description scrubbed of contact details and long numbers, and ChatGPT needing OpenID Connect turned off or the approval page fails. Everything else was held with its class owner named: WisePPC to the Amazon seller and ads entries, Torvex to ad analytics, FlowRunner to n8n, Taskriz to PingRoom, Android Texter to the SMS gateways, Merit Ukrainian Law held because its tool table was not verified this pass, STRG held on a one-line listing and a 401, and Faxbeep, relvectors, Ava Advisor, Motion Reel, post2all, Harbor, Screwtape.ai, VidFare, PepBank, emissaoja, Keysrs, work-access-tools, pagenull, Datacircle, the five CrakSEO submissions, QuotedPart, FixMyPrompt, Holdbird and CorpusFetch held on vertical, thinness or single-author grounds. Core listing check: mcpservers.org still carries /servers/corpusiq-io in the canonical while the detail page answers the same 403 that refuses /all, Glama answers 200 on /mcp/connectors/io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp, the official registry holds io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp 1.0.0 as active with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote and a 30+ description that stays drift against a 40+ catalog, and mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404 and the paid route declined. Counts: guide tree 1,104 directories before this pass and 1,106 after, 1,247 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,249 after, mcpservers.org canonical 19,513 against 19,513, mcp.so 172 timestamped cards and 140 card objects with the newest at 2026-11-06T02:14:00.852Z on both reads, one registry record resolved and zero on three searches for the load planning vendor, two endpoint probes both 401.

Midday sweep November 2 2026, fired seven hours after the night pass in a window where the delta sat in the submission window rather than the feeds. The mcp.so recentServers block carried 30 cards with a date and the newest at 2026-11-02T14:39:24Z against 2026-11-02T09:04:11Z at the night stamp, so five cards sat above it and all five resolved to covered classes: paperjoy sends handwritten postcards inside Poland, 442ball serves football club power ratings, builders-in-fintech is a fintech news and funding feed, eddyter is an editor integration and forge-by-ui8 is a hosted agent front-end from a design-asset vendor. The mcpservers.org /all page repeated its recorded pattern for a fourth pass, the first fetch returning 18,732 with the previous page of thirty slugs and the second fetch, cache busted with a nanosecond stamp and a different user agent, returning 18,887 with the page turned over, so the read whose counter moves is the live one. The issue window moved furthest, 36 submissions landing on chatmcp/mcpso between #6585 at 04:09:42Z and #6620 at 16:36:30Z, and the whole window was read with bodies in one authenticated call. One arrival was catalogued. Versum MCP - https://versum.suverse.io/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP and keyless for every read, initialize answering HTTP 200 with serverInfo versum-catalog 1.6.0 and tools/list returning all 13 tools in 50,179 bytes, and six tools were called live rather than quoted. list_niches returned the whole index in one object: 128 trades, 5,398 cards and 9,300 businesses, each trade carrying a coverage state and the city zones behind it with the date last passed, restaurant at 783 cards over 1,042 businesses and partial for a printed reason while florist is 183 over 316 and complete. search_catalog for pizza in Tampa answered 12 matches inside 15 miles and handed back a real shelf: Green Bench Brewing Co. at 0.3 miles, its phone number, FOUR CHEESE PIZZA at 12.95 and Pepperoni at 14.50. get_offering returns the price as a claim with the shop's own page as the evidence, price_state confirmed on basis published from semantic_html with the quote field carrying the dollar figure, and it sets availability_state to unknown on basis not published beside it, so what a shop charges and whether it is in stock arrive as two separately labelled facts. find_business with needed_by resolved the timestamp to open_at and returned a task card with state confirmed and the reasoning that the shop is open at 19:00 by its published hours, plus the five cheapest items priced. quote_order answered placed false with reason no_public_cart and said what it had done: the shop's own public cart priced the order in a session of its own which was emptied afterwards, only the delivery address was sent and nothing was kept. It earns a guide because nothing in the catalogue reads a local shop's own shelf, the three neighbours on business identity being GBPly for your own profile, Listings API for publishing out to directories and GoodLeads for new-business filing leads, with Undercart the nearest neighbour and covering online Shopify stores rather than the shop with a Squarespace menu and a phone number. Held: Local Business Facts (Agentric) driven keyless to confidence 0.86 with per-field source and method on every fact and held on class as business enrichment by URL already carried by Vibe Prospecting and Leadbay, with a promotion test recorded for any wanted-by field needing a confidence score; Sumora on the lead-generation class; Evalmee on education authoring; Peerlytics on consumer crypto analytics; Binnacle on developer tooling; Narva and Raywake on saturated media generation; AlphaPrime on the trading and market slice carried by Altair, ValuEdge, fAlpha, BDE and the nine EDGAR surfaces; LetsBot and Perisclaw on the saturated messaging class; Faxend and Tempost each submitted twice inside a two-hour window as a resubmission pattern rather than four arrivals; fixRAgent as already catalogued at the October 14 midday pass; and the Chris Pereira, iMpact and Global Connect Show desks as single vendor or single person promotional surfaces. On /all the unledgered slugs were hologramxyz, whose detail route answers a 404 shell so the listing is real and the page is not published yet, perisclaw-mcp and nova-civai-co-agent-product-admin, with every other slug resolving to an existing guide directory. All five tracked listing surfaces were re-probed because the night pass recorded them as not run: CorpusIQ is live on mcpservers.org at /servers/corpusiq-io, live on Smithery through the registry API at qualifiedName benoit-p/Cprusiq with displayName CorpusIQ while the HTML page route 404s and a control test on two unrelated published servers 404s identically because the web directory migrated to an Arcade-powered directory so every old server route went with it, a recorded migration and not a delisting, live on Glama both as the connector io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp on the newer /mcp/connectors/ route and as CorpusIQ/corpusiq-docs on /mcp/servers/, active in the official registry as io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote, and still not listed on mcp.so with all four direct slugs at 404. Counts: mcpservers.org /all proxy read 30 slugs with the counter at 18,887 against 18,732 stale, mcp.so recentServers 30 cards with the newest at 2026-11-02T14:39:24Z, issue window #6585 to #6620, guide tree 1,084 server entries before this pass and 1,085 after. Supplement pass an hour later on the 11:00 MST tick, treated as a supplement rather than a second read of the same surfaces: the only new submissions were #6621 Publish MCP, #6622 norc and #6623 Lingard Vocab, all held on covered classes, and one reversal was made with a reason attached. AttriKit MCP was catalogued as the first entry that closes the loop from ad spend to app install to subscription revenue to a budget decision: stdio through npx @attrkit/mcp, published as 2.0.1 on npm with the MIT repository KamyarTah