alone identifies the site and records no visits. What it answers is the input side of the AI-visibility question this catalogue has only ever measured from the answer side: whether Googlebot reached the important pages with visits, journeys and sitemap gaps, what AI bots are reading as visit trails plus llms.txt coverage match or miss, and which bots hit HTTP errors, robots conflicts or a forged user agent, the last checked by reverse DNS on Pro and above; the vendor's own limit is quoted in the guide, visit records and policy signals rather than search rankings or model-training proof. The pricing line matters: the free plan is 1 site and 100 crawl visits a month with crawl analysis only, and llms.txt coverage, sitemap coverage, bot authenticity and the crawl-like-a-bot simulation all start at Pro at 20 dollars a month, with the integrations panel at Pro+ 40 dollars and yearly billing at ten times monthly. It earns a guide because the answer side is held three ways and the input side none, NM Signals auditing how crawlers would see a URL, AIO.GEO auditing structural readiness and dry-running fixes, and Encited mining Search Console and answer-engine visibility, none of which can say whether the crawler came back after a migration or whether the fetch returned a 403. Held with measurements: Gamebeast from the feed is the official server for one game LiveOps platform and is a single-vendor vertical with a promotion test recorded; workload.zero answered keyless initialize 200 as workload-zero 2.1.0 with 149 tools spanning profile, projects and budgets, clients, tasks, timers, goals, deals, quotes, quote-to-invoice and revenue, the widest surface in the window and a hosted German business suite whose slices are carried by Deskhand, NOVA for Kommo, Finwise, Reciba and Volanea; GameshipKit answered keyless 200 as gameshipkit 1.0.0 with five tools over 69 browser tools for pixel art and store assets and is outside operator scope; Links as a Service answered 401 invalid_token and is a Danish link marketplace with 150k publisher domains at publisher cost plus 20 percent, held because the link-building slice is carried by RankControl and MentionAgent and what remains is a checkout over bought inventory rather than data that is read; Smitline is a self-hosted open-source server for phone calls and Zoom, Teams and Meet attendance, held on two carried classes at once, voice by PlaceCall and meeting notes by Granola, ParrotNotes, Tactiq and Lavox; UX Pilot answered 401 -32001 API key is required and drives UI design on its own canvas; EZ@Work answered 401 and is the freelancer version of the invoicing and time slice. Held on class without a probe because the precedent is settled: astraeye-labs on stock research beside Altair, ValuEdge, fAlpha, BDE and the EDGAR surfaces, exclusive-digits on number inventory, orinyx as a healthcare vertical beside TMSClinics and SleepStudies, lingviko outside scope, snapwidget as a website embed rather than a data surface, Tabula and Kipurse and I Am Wallet and Haris Guardian on agent payments and crypto beside FiatDock, CoinVello, SnapEX Pay and Spectra, Dopamyn on crypto audience intelligence, run.zero on developer PaaS, Mobilebox on device farms, UberLLM and Sirv on media generation, Postly on physical mail, Same Day Website Builder on the site-builder class, CallAI SEO on the twenty-guide SEO class, AI SENSE as an aggregator of 77 free utilities, the three tidybytetools utilities as local developer tools, and seam, Markdown Pipeline, ipvolt and AdminHub for Telegram on diff review, Jira-to-Markdown sync, proxy set-up and hosted Telegram publishing. One execution note is recorded because it will recur: a 10:00 MST attempt on the same surfaces stopped mid-run without committing, so its canonical capture and its /all pages 1 to 5 were reused and the window delta was recomputed as a fresh set difference on the two files rather than read out of the dead run's output. Counts: guide tree 1,098 directories before this pass and 1,099 after, 1,242 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,243 after, mcp.so 124 objects with the newest at 2026-11-04T14:37:59Z, mcpservers.org /all at 19,342 then 19,344, a canonical set difference of five additions and zero removals from 19,339 to 19,344, and six endpoint probes with two answering 200 and four answering 401.

Correction recorded on the same day, after the 10:00 MST midday row and before the evening pass: the first merged version of this supplement's guide claimed that the catalogue held the AI-visibility answer side and the input side none. That was wrong, and the 10:00 pass had already said so when it held NMOS on the crawl-visibility class citing SEOcrawl AI, pathwren and IndexLinks crawl receipts. IndexLinks has read verified crawler visits with timestamps since October 6 and pathwren verifies crawler IPs against operator-published ranges, so the guide now names both as nearest neighbours and states the difference instead of asserting the slice was missing: IndexLinks proves a crawl for pages sent to its own submission network one page at a time on a plan priced by submitted pages from 49 dollars a month, while one beacon on NMOS logs every crawler that reaches any page including pages nobody submitted, with sitemap gaps, robots conflicts, reverse-DNS authenticity, SSL health and a free tier. The reversal of the 10:00 hold is therefore on the surface rather than the vendor, and it is recorded rather than silent. Lesson for the next pass, which is the reason this note exists: a class claim is a grep over every neighbour the prior pass named, run before the page is written, not an impression formed from the candidates in front of you.


Evening sweep November 4 2026, eleven hours after the midday pass, and the shape was the reverse of the midday read: the feeds barely moved and the directory did. mcpservers.org went from 19,344 to 19,515 on both reads through the reader proxy, 171 entries, and its newest page shared no slug with the thirty the midday pass dispositioned; 120 slugs were read across pages 1 to 4 and 113 were unledgered on a first slug pass. mcp.so produced 26 server objects with the newest at 2026-11-04T23:13:21Z (Actora MCP) and only 4 cards above the midday stamp. The submission window carried 17 items between #6746 Scrape.ly at 18:02:07Z and #6762 Emploist at 2026-11-05T03:51:45Z, read with bodies in one authenticated call, one of them #6761 AGNT an MCP client rather than a server, so the window is 16 arrivals. The finding of the pass is about crossref rather than about servers: the 171-entry wave reads as 113 new slugs and as a handful of new products, because the directory is ingesting a backlog while the product-name form of the same items was already dispositioned by the night pass (the -docs-mcp documentation fleet of Cartrelay, Hirelabs, Ziva.sh, Teddit.io, Echoly, Skael, Webclaw, Recl and Rainbrand; the theluckystrike calculator four; the antevo.ch four; the tidybytetools trio) and thirteen more match this window or the one before it directly. Two entries were catalogued and both were driven rather than quoted. ProveCart at https://api.provecart.com/mcp answered a keyless initialize 200 as provecart 1.0.2 with all 10 tools listed; provecart_scoreboard and provecart_certification_info were called live and returned real payloads while the three check tools refused with one sentence naming the integrator X-API-Key they need, so the check payload is schema-read and not measured. The three check tools compare what an agent built against the customer's structured mandate and return a signed MATCH, REVIEW or BLOCK before the payment, with a non-MATCH answer carrying the Agent Correction Format: a corrections array of dimension, action, expected, actual and reason, a retry budget and a sealed evidence pointer. The mandates are the substance, 18 fields on an order including max_total_price, merchant_allowlist, merchant_blocklist, max_quantity, variant_constraints, price_basis, expires_at and a period_budget with its own window, 26 on a booking including airport_substitution, date_flex_days, fare_terms and the connection limits, 17 on a reservation including time_tolerance_minutes, party_size_max and max_deposit. The scoreboard read live is the argument for the exam: two agents at 100.0 over 29 checks with certification CURRENT to 2027-02-02 and two audit probes at 13.8 and 11.1, with origin separating external, house and audit runs; 80 or above certifies, a pass is CURRENT for 90 days, renewal is a newly generated exam and a pass yields an Open Badges 3.0 credential under did:web:api.provecart.com. lookfirst at github.com/Aethelgard-Systems/lookfirst is Apache-2.0 and was installed here and driven: lookfirst 0.2.1 against a README that says 0.2.0 pre-1.0, and the offline demo run twice, the approval run returning status executed with approved_by elicitation:mcp and readback ok while the fake bank moved 1,250.00 to 1,129.50 EUR for a 120.50 EUR transfer, the denial run returning status denied with the channel named and the balance untouched, both exiting 0. Five behaviours earn the guide: the decision table fails closed with readOnlyHint allowing and every write, unannotated tool and unknown tool confirming while deny never executes; the approval is bound to the arguments by a per-call HMAC token and the preview's args_sha256 with a 403 on mismatch and a timeout treated as denial; the write is verified by read-back reported as ok, unklar or fehlgeschlagen in structuredContent.lookfirst; the log is an Ed25519 hash chain where verify-log walked 20 signed entries to OK and then returned TAMPERED at line 6 after the demo rewrote the decision entry; and the result is masked before the model sees it, the client receiving [[IBAN_...]] placeholders that resolve inside the gate while an invented one is refused. The limits are the vendor's own: pre-1.0 with 0 stars and no field record, an autonomous client can self-approve through elicitation unless confirm.elicitation is off and the page is isolated at the network level, the page has no login and is for 127.0.0.1, an HTTP token is authentication not encryption, Windows is untested, and the mask is a deterministic filter that misses split IBANs, zero-width text, Base64 secrets and db_password. Held with measurements: mailers-scan-api, one keyless scan_domain returning a score against maxScore 80 plus MX, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, rDNS and domain age at 60 requests an hour with no DNSBL leg, held on class behind how.is with its 17 checks, Mamba's fingerprint and Leadgen; the antevo.ch four dispositioned together, Tremor Watch held on the note that 35 of 176 volatility and equity pairs broke at 3.1x normal, the 184th most unsettled of 1,348 Fridays since 2001, against portfolio-specific risk carried by PairBook and openInvest, with a per-portfolio exposure call recorded as the promotion test; Antevo Trademark held behind Goalie and IP Defender; 1ToolRing on the data-aggregator class; workbook-tools-mcp behind the SheetsFinance spreadsheet slice; uptrack, invisit and pdf-a11y on their carried classes; and the four feed cards Actora, Arsen, Circles and Airport Pickups London held as one vertical each. Three antevo.ch paths answered 405 to a keyless initialize, so Tremor Watch was dispositioned on its published figures rather than a session. Counts: guide tree 1,099 directories before this pass and 1,101 after, 1,243 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,245 after.

Midday sweep November 5 2026, seven hours after the night pass, and the shape was flat on both named surfaces. The twelve-sitemap canonical came back at 19,513 server URLs, the same number as the 04:31 MST capture, with 2 additions and 2 removals where both removals pair exactly with an addition whose namespace prefix was dropped - ad/mcp-project-helper became mcp-project-helper and dg/pohoda-mcp became pohoda-mcp - so nothing entered or left the ecosystem in the window. The locale strip is now mandatory before any diff: 43,181 URLs carry the locale inline as /de/servers/ rather than /servers/de/, and a naive set difference reads that as 43,179 additions. mcp.so was parsed from a direct fetch at 172 cards with the newest at 2026-11-05T06:47:30Z, which is the night pass's own stamp, so the feed carried zero new cards; mcpservers.org /all refused every read again, 403 to a direct browser-agent fetch and 401 03 bad IP reputation through the reader proxy, which is now the standing condition rather than an incident. The submission queue was the whole window: 36 items from #6773 Desktop Steward to #6808 DataXAPI, read with bodies in one authenticated call, and 21 of them are one author's fleet, mambalabsdev from #6782 to #6802, covering an email verifier, a whois lookup, a Substack scraper, a Reddit thread scraper, a Threads keyword search, an ATS jobs feed, a LinkedIn jobs feed, a Product Hunt launches feed, recent funding rounds, an app-store review monitor, an AI answer visibility tracker and six list-builder tools, every one of them in a class the catalog already carries, so the fleet is held as one line under the single-author rule. One arrival was catalogued. Korzy MCP - https://api.korzy.co/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP and registered as co.korzy/korzy 1.0.0 at 2026-11-05T13:41:35Z, and a keyless initialize returns 401 with 'Sign in or provide a valid Korzy credential', so the tier is documentation rather than a driven session. The sixteen read-only tools are read from the vendor's own table: parcel and address search, water and sewer service areas with the treatment plants that serve them, one water/sewer/treatment/gas/fiber record, power plants with generators, total and available TRANSFER CAPACITY IN MW for a regional grid interface, environmental layers including flood zones and wetlands plus nearby cleanup sites, logistics context, data-center projects with capacity evidence and a dated timeline, regional energy prices and fuel mix, coal receipts linking mines to plants, terrain coverage and slope/elevation over a parcel. The credits are the honest part and they come from the OpenAPI document at korzy.co/openapi.json, 193,888 bytes with an x-korzy-credits block on all 34 routes: an address search or a parcel record is 1 credit, a point context is 2 with a 1 to 10 range priced per ten records, include_owner doubles the parcel and site calls, a utility/project/environment/logistics record is 1 to 2, a coal shipments read is 10 and a plant history or regional energy read is 50. Professional is 49 dollars a month or 490 a year for 3,000 credits with extra at 16 dollars per 1,000, Business is 199 a month or 1,990 a year with unlimited seats, and there is no free tier because the endpoint answers 402 subscription_required without an active plan even though three summary tools cost zero credits. It earns a guide because the property entries here read what the record says - PropRaven over 191.3M parcels, Placestack on parcel and zoning, Hercules on ownership and mortgages, DFX on commercial debt - and none answers whether the site can be SERVED, which is the question before an option payment; DC Hub and the energy entry read the same grid question at market level and this is the parcel-level read. Held with the class named: JaKonto (#6807) driven keyless to 200 as jakonto with five read-only tools over e-conomic, Dinero and Billy and held on the geo-niche accounting class set by DokladBot, Taokeh, Kvickd, Amore Fortnox, Mighty, Zeno, Grand Livre, Nextesy and Pohoda; Stackurity (#6804) on security inventory beside VulX Watch; getwork.dev (#6805) on jobs data beside ATS Jobs, CareJobs.Now, Applystead and RobotTraining.jobs; Growth Radar (#6780) on the saturated visibility class; Shipbook (#6774) on observability; EZO Watcher (#6777) on monitoring beside Cronitor, Runheed and uptrack; Desktop Steward (#6773) on local files and agent infrastructure; EXTREMELY agency (#6781) on agent orchestration; OMX for Hyperliquid (#6775) and Solana Alpha x402 (#6803) on trading and agent payments; RoomLab (#6779) on media generation; Feedough Prompt Generator (#6778) as prompt tooling; Piratex (#6776) as a single-market creator vertical; DataXAPI (#6808) on scraping and social data beside LurkAPI and the Apify-actor hold. Core listings re-probed in the same pass: mcpservers.org still carries /servers/corpusiq-io in the canonical while the detail page answers 403, Glama answers 200 on /mcp/connectors/io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp with the CorpusIQ title and the 40+ description, the official registry carries io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote and a 30+ description that is now drift to correct at the next publish, Smithery could not be confirmed because the registry API errored twice and /servers/ returned 308 then 404 on redirect which is a routing change and never a delisting, and mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404 and the paid route declined. Counts: guide tree 1,102 directories before this pass and 1,103 after, 1,246 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,247 after.

Late morning sweep November 5 2026, one hour after the midday pass, and the two named surfaces answered in opposite ways. The mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap canonical came back set-identical to the 04:31 MST capture: 19,513 server URLs, zero additions and zero removals, the first exact empty diff this surface has produced after a week of namespace-prefix shuffles. Two counting notes go with it: the sitemap index now carries static.xml beside the twelve server and priority maps, so a raw union reads 28,851 URLs and 9,338 of them are marketing, topic and search pages, and only the /servers/ subset of 19,513 is the server universe; and /all returned 403 for the fourth consecutive pass, a standing condition rather than an incident. The mcp.so homepage carried the pass's whole delta and carried it only on the second read: the plain fetch returned 80 cards with the newest at 2026-11-05T06:47:30Z, the stamp the midday pass had already dispositioned, which reads as a flat feed, while a cache-busted read of the same page returned the same 80 cards plus one at 2026-11-05T17:29:38.960Z, so the plain read was 31 minutes stale and the two-read rule written for the three-hour ticks now applies at every interval. One server was catalogued. Konshus MCP - https://konshus.ai/api/mcp is remote stateless Streamable HTTP, registered as ai.konshus/memory 1.0.0 at 2026-11-05T17:35:03Z six minutes after the directory card, OAuth 2.1 with PKCE S256, authorization_code and refresh_token grants, a dynamic client registration endpoint and a single scope vault:rw. A keyless initialize returns 401 -32001 with the message that the server is stateless and every request must carry a bearer, and a probe token returns 401 Invalid or expired token, so the tier is documentation rather than a driven session. The eleven tools are read from the vendor's own table in four scope groups: summary get_whisper, get_briefing, get_persona_summary and get_vault_stats; recall search_atoms with as_of for a point-in-time view, search_artifacts over raw sources, recall_past_self, explain_what_you_know_about as a narrative with citations and whats_changed_since as a standup; capture log_signal, the only write and the reason the scope is read-write rather than read-only; and full mirror get_mega_briefing. It earns a guide on a gap rather than a neighbour, because the five memory entries here are agent working memory, Agentic Memory over Redis with FIFO handoff, AIS Memory with a W3C DID identity, MCP Long-Term Memory over Neo4j, Linksee local-first with a forgetting curve and SPM project-scoped with context packs, and none of them ingests a person's ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok history across 25 sources with 22 live, Google Calendar in beta and Apple Health plus Spotify announced, nor serves it back with a source and a confidence label on every distilled atom. Pricing is read off the pricing page as a five-tier ladder: Ember free with 50 memories and journal-or-paste ingestion only, Spark 49 dollars a year for 250 to 500 active memories and 10 GB over a one-year window, Founding 149 dollars a year for 2,500 to 10,000 memories and 50 GB over three years with all imports, Counsel 299 dollars a year for up to 35,000 memories and 100 GB over seven years, and Counsel Pro 599 dollars a year with a 300 GB vault and a lifetime window, against a founding cohort the vendor says has 1,456 of 4,000 memberships left. Limits recorded in the guide: a consumer product rather than a business data connector, vault:rw as the only scope so per-scope token issuance is the control that matters, encryption and discretion claims that cannot be checked from outside, self-reported usage figures printed on the vendor's own page at 99.81 percent seven-day uptime, 12,055 calls, 448 connected clients and a 0.9 second p50, and one vault per member with no team or per-client separation. Nothing else was held because nothing else arrived. Core listing check: mcpservers.org still carries /servers/corpusiq-io in the canonical while the detail page answers the same 403 that refuses /all, Glama answers 200 on /mcp/connectors/io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp, the official registry holds io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp 1.0.0 as active with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote and a 30+ description that stays drift against a 40+ catalog, and mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404 and the paid route declined. Counts: guide tree 1,103 directories before this pass and 1,104 after, 1,247 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,248 after, mcpservers.org canonical 19,513 against 19,513, mcp.so 80 cards on both reads with the cache-busted newest at 2026-11-05T17:29:38.960Z, one registry record resolved, two endpoint probes both 401.
Midday sweep November 7 2026, fired on the 10:00 MST tick six hours after a night pass that proved the canonical flat by arithmetic, and the same surface moved this time: the twelve-sitemap universe went from 19,859 to 19,898 distinct server URLs, 40 additions and 1 removal, from 63,231 raw loc entries across 12 server maps with the inline locale prefixes stripped. Three of the 40 were prior dispositions confirmed by context rather than substring: itulo/eu-nordic-open-data-mcp on the Apify actor distribution hold from the October 27 sweep, tankucukhas/spacepal-mcp on the macOS Spaces consumer hold from the night pass, and patentref-mcp on the patent and IP class carried by Patsnap and LegalCode. The 37 survivors went to the official MCP registry, which returned a name and description match for 22, and six of those were wrong-product matches caught by reading the description rather than the name (asinrating, eckari, getle, rallyprop, avasis, everydaysecurity), every one a shared token rather than an identity. mcpservers.org /all and every detail page refused again, 403 direct and 401 03 through the reader proxy, the standing condition since November 4. The mcp.so homepage was read direct with a browser user agent and gzip decoded, 188 createdAt occurrences across 148 cards, newest 2026-11-07T16:50:15.825Z (Fulfy Plus), 5 cards strictly above the night stamp and one at it. The queue carried six numbers from 6893 to 6898 with bodies in one authenticated call, all arrivals. One server was catalogued: West Kite MCP at https://app.westkite.com/mcp answered a keyless initialize 401 with SIGN_IN_REQUIRED and a WWW-Authenticate header naming https://app.westkite.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp plus a ten-scope list separating reads from writes, and that document answered 200 with 15 scopes, the authorization server and its own documentation URL, so the tier is documented from the server's own contract. It carries 107 million US parcels across 1,787 counties in 2