ment vertical, Agentic Kingdoms as a consumer game, Fezola and GhosterMail on email from the queue. Six probes, one keyless 200, one protected-resource 200, four refusals. Core listing check measured: the canonical carries /servers/corpusiq-io and /servers/corpusiq/corpusiq-docs, the detail page answers 403 by edge policy rather than delisting, Glama answers 200 on the connector route, all four mcp.so slugs still 404, and smithery returned an error payload so no state is inferred. Guide tree 1,112 directories before and 1,113 after, 1,255 entries before and 1,256 after.

Evening sweep November 7 2026, fired on the 21:00 MST tick ten hours after the midday supplement, and the largest surface moved this time: the mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap universe went from 19,898 distinct server URLs at 11:00 to 20,000, from 63,359 raw loc entries across 12 server maps with 43,344 inline locale prefixes stripped. Against the 03:00 night capture that is 142 additions and 1 removal, and since the midday pass had already dispositioned 40 of them, 100 slugs were genuinely undispositioned in this window; two of the 142, DocPin and West Kite, were catalogued earlier today and only entered the sitemaps afterwards. mcpservers.org /all refused again, 403 direct and 401 through the reader proxy, the standing condition since November 4. The mcp.so homepage was read twice, plain and cache-busted, with identical results: 172 createdAt stamps, 129 cards, newest 2026-11-08T06:00:20.000Z, and 24 cards strictly above the 11:00 stamp of 2026-11-07T16:50:15.825Z, of which 19 carry consecutive stamps from 06:00:01Z to 06:00:20Z and read as one scheduled bulk publish two hours ahead of the pass clock, while five were ordinary arrivals (getcheapgames, pingstack, simplyboost, sell-my-data-to-ai, simvito-esim). The queue carried 19 numbers from 6902 to 6922 with 6905 and 6913 absent, all arrivals. Four servers were catalogued, and they line up on one idea without having been chosen for it. PointRover MCP at https://pointrover.com/mcp answered a keyless initialize 401 invalid_token naming its discovery document, and that document answered 200 with one scope read:tenant, so the tier is documented from the contract; nine read-only tools over a per-business board built in about an hour and checked every twelve hours, with pointrover_changes_since taking a board_version and pointrover_receipt returning the record behind a single figure, at 79 dollars a business a month after a 14-day trial. Patchwell MCP answered keyless 200 as Patchwell 1.30.0 with five tools, and the evidence chain is the product: cleaning returns stats, a 0.30 to 0.998 quality score, a per-change log with row, column, before, after and rule, and a replayable recipe, research puts a source link on each sentence and lists unconfirmed claims in gaps, transcription lists every hallucination-guard removal, at 0.008 dollars an audio minute, 0.50 per 1,000 rows and 0.15 a research answer with a 1 dollar key and no card. DeskHand MCP answered keyless 200 as deskhand 1.0.0 with 30 tools and a policy preamble the server writes for the agent, and the controls are the finding: one key per agent with scopes, an append-only audit log with before and after, revert one action or a whole run, approval as a switch per agent, and a built-in dry_run identity so simulate_campaign renders what would go out before launch_campaign refuses on named blockers, free during early access and 19 euros a month on Pro. eDiscovery Decoder MCP answered keyless 200 as ediscovery-decoder-news-calc 0.1.0 with 15 tools, 13 of them usable, deterministic review statistics (elusion, sample size, TAR recall, prevalence, control-set recall, cutoff comparison, validation-plan QC) with no account, no key and aggregate counts only, stated by the vendor as an educational non-commercial preview. Held with the class owner named: a1lane on the saturated social publishing class, Bobwork email warmup on Warmerly, Lexpact on UK contract generation, mutalaa on the regional legal class, the four illyism packs as one fleet, adplug and adwarp on ads, eight media-generation slugs, twenty-one developer and infrastructure slugs, api-lilambd on the Apify-actor distribution hold, ezverify and mailveri on email verification, LinkJolt on affiliate operations, and from the queue Conductor on LedgerCrossing for QuickBooks Desktop, Threatist on Bot Wire, Stackurity and cve-now, Foresight Planner on Retirement Atlas and Meridary, Free YT Bulk Transcripts on the transcript class, and Mishmar and Umless on the saturated trading and med