Early morning sweep November 11 2026, fired on the 03:00 MST tick six hours after the evening read, and the two surfaces disagreed in a way that is measurable rather than asserted. The mcpservers.org sitemap index answered 200 and named the same fifteen maps, twelve of them carrying /servers/ URLs, and every one of those twelve carried exactly the per-map raw count of the 21:00 MST pass (priority 299; 7,588 / 5,948 / 6,518 / 6,744 / 6,952 / 6,756 / 9,351 / 6,588 / 4,031 / 2,604 / 601) for 63,995 entries, so no URL was added or removed overnight; across all fifteen maps the raw <url> total was 77,396 once static.xml (822) and skills.xml (12,579) are counted. Normalising to the first two path segments after /servers/ gave 20,405 distinct keys, 18,588 of them carrying a lastmod, the newest 2026-11-10T23:48:14Z, nine above 22:50Z and zero at or after the 04:14Z cutoff; the six-key gap against the previous pass's 20,411 is a normalisation difference and is recorded as one, not as removals. The mcp.so homepage answered 200 at 288,585 bytes with 32 card anchors resolving to 30 distinct slugs, 22 of them timestamped, and eight above the cutoff ALL stamped 2026-11-11T08:00Z, which is one scheduled publish batch and not eight discoveries. The official registry was queried for all eight candidates and returned records for six, including a genuine collision where two different products are both listed as unslop (io.github.0design/unslop 0.1.0 and io.github.avivgerz-hue/unslop 2.1.1). The chatmcp submission queue was NOT read this pass because no scripted reader exists for the authenticated session, and that is stated rather than dropped. Three local-first servers were catalogued and each was installed and driven on the host, because a handshake probe measures nothing about a stdio tool: dead-letter 0.4.10 (five tools listed with get_diagnostics the only readOnlyHint true, resources and prompts both zero while advertised, four conversions run showing a duplicated multipart collapsed to one body, an HTML signature preserved as a Markdown table, the date normalised to ISO 8601 UTC from -0500, a tracking pixel RETAINED by default until --strip-tracking-pixels, and --strip-signatures missing the table-shaped signature; PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 with no commercial licence published and no mailbox connection); vibe-shield 2.1.2 (grade F 0/100 with five critical in 26 ms over 80 rules, the hardcoded credential redacted in its own output, score.ceiling critical limit 29, exit codes plain 1 / fail-on 1 / json 1 / clean control 0, and audit-skills across twelve rules catching VSB-AGENT-002 env exfiltration while flagging neither concealment instruction); ctxvault 0.9.1 package with serverInfo 1.30.0 (seventeen tools listed, a full episodic lifecycle run where two statements both stayed open before supersede closed the origin at the exact microsecond the replacement opened with a superseded-by pointer and no deletion, one directory and one episodes.db per vault, and a 5.9 GB install footprint because sentence-transformers and chromadb are hard dependencies). Five held with measured reasons: caprock, unslop, usb-rea, tandoor-recipe-mcp and agent-vscreen. Landed as PR #290, squash 3c401aa12a, frontmatter green in 2m19s; deploy COMPLETE with build-info.json serving that sha at 10:23:57Z and five URLs 200 cache-busted no-slash on docs plus two on the www proxy. Guide tree 1,143 directories before this pass and 1,146 after, 144 loose entries, 1,290 catalog entries.

Midday sweep November 11 2026, fired on the 10:00 MST tick seven hours after the early-morning read, and this window is the mirror image of the overnight one: the mcpservers.org canonical GREW by 294 server keys where the overnight pass was flat to the entry count. Index at /sitemap.xml answered 200 naming fifteen maps, twelve carrying /servers/ URLs, all twelve fetched individually: 64,336 raw <loc> entries, every one under /servers/, giving 20,702 distinct keys after normalising to the first two path segments, 58,893 carrying a lastmod with the newest 2026-11-11T11:25:56Z and 244 distinct keys at or after the 04:14Z cutoff. Diff against the 21:00 MST Nov 10 capture kept on disk (20,411 keys) gave 294 additions and 3 removals, and the removals are the %23 fragment normalisation pair recorded for the tenth time (ahmedkhaleel2004/gitdiagram, orcasecurity/orca-skills, podop29/shotpipe-mcp) rather than products leaving. The growth landed in three maps and nowhere else: servers/11 from 601 to 954, servers/10 from 2,604 to 2,606, servers/8 from 6,588 to 6,589, every other map byte-stable against the overnight count, which is why a per-map count is a faster arrival signal than a total. 125 of the 294 are named cohorts, not arrivals: 41 Company Atlas country and trade slugs already carried by a catalogued guide, 27 documentation mirrors, 20 Cotlet per-app connectors already resolved into one catalogued entry, 17 -myagents-click mirror pages, 5 Mamba Labs Apify items, 3 avivgerz-hue items disposed this morning, 3 kindoflost, 3 msg2ai, 2 getitdone, 2 truetest, 2 t4dhg. Three of the remainder turned out to be this catalog own work arriving in the canonical: bigcactuslabs/dead-letter, filippo-venturini/ctxvault and dspv/caprock, the three servers the 03:00 MST pass shipped and held. The mcp.so feed answered 200 at 142,742 bytes with 32 distinct cards and 4 above the 10:20Z cutoff (anyreach 16:06Z, lampwick-error-tracking-app-monitoring 16:04Z, kwery 15:08Z, live-web-data 15:01Z), timestamps read from the title attribute and converted from UTC because the display string is UTC in 12-hour text and reads seven hours wrong as local time. The submission window was #7129 to #7150, 22 arrivals with no gaps, read in one authenticated call. Three servers catalogued, all three operator questions a paper process answers badly. bullion-price-check (registry com.bullionpricecheck/bullion-price-check, 2.0.0 published and 2.1.0 served, which is drift in the reverse direction from usual) is keyless end to end with 27 tools all readOnlyHint true and six calls driven: spot gold 4,002.80 silver 52.38 platinum 1,551 at a 76.42 ratio with a freshness block at 70 minutes against a 120 threshold and palladium declared out of scope; the dealer ladder for one silver round ran 4.57 percent over melt at the low to 20.59 percent at the top, an 8.39 USD spread, with three Partner labels ranking 2, 4 and 5 as live proof that a partner pays to list and never to rank, and two exclusions stated with reasons (out of stock; a price 471 minutes old against a 60-minute source limit); the Premium Index puts the median dealer at two to two and a half times the lowest premium on the same five silver products; true_cost priced ten units delivered at 3,316.50 each with a 1,120 card surcharge on top; bullion_sales_tax answers per state with rule text and partial and taxable statuses rather than a binary flag; and fair_offer_check rejects a product string its own schema advertises, refusing to invent a number. touristpads (registry com.touristpads/touristpads 1.0.0, keyless, three tools with only request_quote a write) priced a six-iPad two-router three-day order to 2,407.00 SGD where equipment was 68.6 percent and the calendar 31.4 percent (delivery 106.80, after hours 150, Sunday leg 500) and then volunteered a Monday collection at 1,907.00 SGD, exactly 500 less, with the initialize instructions telling the assistant to surface it; the estimate says no quote has been issued and an after-hours charge needs the customer agreement first, and the rules publish the levers (280 SGD minimum, 75 per 30 minutes outside 9am to 6pm per leg, 500 for a Sunday leg, 8 percent off at 2,000 and 10 percent at 3,000 applied automatically, location surcharges added at signing rather than quoted). photoproof (registry io.photoproof/mcp 1.0.0) is recorded at the OAuth evidence tier: a keyless initialize answered 401 with resource_metadata and scope galleries:read galleries:write, both metadata documents read in full, two scopes in one read and write pair with dynamic registration, code as the only response type, none among the token auth methods and S256 only for PKCE; the product is proofing rather than selling, with a client selecting, rejecting and commenting without an account and pressing Confirm, Lightroom paste codes, finals up to 4 GB per file, and plans checked 2026-11-11 from Free at 0 to Studio at 19 per month, in euro with VAT and no commission. Held with named reasons: ouncescout class-covered by the bullion entry just shipped, holdingsintel on trading saturation, mcp-slim on a registry name collision with a different package (io.github.lennney/mcp-slim-guard advertises 83 percent on one record and 76 on another) worth measuring later at one number, sebbi because its own compliance-check figure moves 680 to 739 to 755 across three published versions in a day, the agent-security group behind vibe-shield, 3dCMS and ViralMint on class, Umpirix and HTMLRadar as developer and document surfaces, livecrm October 14, the x402 group, wishpond salescloser, dundas and the two Metabase slugs on BI, t4dhg holded and eudamed, the social publishing group, pinnfeed, narwhalapi, the AI-visibility group, the Apify actor group, the consumer games, gridradar, guarapay, whoisfreaks (no registry record, recorded as unattributed rather than inferred) and 27 documentation mirrors by class. Gates green before the push with the venv python: validate_frontmatter 7,036 files,